.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH craft 1  "craft " 
.SH NAME
craft \- Encode a PacketSpec from field flags → stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcraft\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-iface\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-\-no\-autofill\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-layer\fR] [\fB\-\-payload\fR] [\fB\-\-eth\-dst\fR] [\fB\-\-eth\-src\fR] [\fB\-\-eth\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-arp\-htype\fR] [\fB\-\-arp\-ptype\fR] [\fB\-\-arp\-hlen\fR] [\fB\-\-arp\-plen\fR] [\fB\-\-arp\-oper\fR] [\fB\-\-arp\-sha\fR] [\fB\-\-arp\-spa\fR] [\fB\-\-arp\-tha\fR] [\fB\-\-arp\-tpa\fR] [\fB\-\-vlan\-pcp\fR] [\fB\-\-vlan\-dei\fR] [\fB\-\-vlan\-vid\fR] [\fB\-\-vlan\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-ver\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-ihl\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-tos\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-total_len\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-flags\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-flags\-df\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-flags\-mf\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-frag_off\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-proto\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-checksum\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-src\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-dst\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv4\-options\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv6\-ver\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv6\-traffic_class\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv6\-flow_label\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv6\-payload_len\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv6\-next_header\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv6\-hop_limit\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv6\-src\fR] [\fB\-\-ipv6\-dst\fR] [\fB\-\-hopopts\-next_header\fR] [\fB\-\-hopopts\-len\fR] [\fB\-\-hopopts\-options\fR] [\fB\-\-dstopts\-next_header\fR] [\fB\-\-dstopts\-len\fR] [\fB\-\-dstopts\-options\fR] [\fB\-\-routing\-next_header\fR] [\fB\-\-routing\-len\fR] [\fB\-\-routing\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-routing\-segs_left\fR] [\fB\-\-routing\-segments\fR] [\fB\-\-frag\-next_header\fR] [\fB\-\-frag\-offset\fR] [\fB\-\-frag\-m\fR] [\fB\-\-frag\-ident\fR] [\fB\-\-ah\-next_header\fR] [\fB\-\-ah\-len\fR] [\fB\-\-ah\-spi\fR] [\fB\-\-ah\-seq\fR] [\fB\-\-ah\-icv\fR] [\fB\-\-esp\-spi\fR] [\fB\-\-esp\-seq\fR] [\fB\-\-icmp\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-icmp\-code\fR] [\fB\-\-icmp\-checksum\fR] [\fB\-\-icmp\-echo\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-icmp\-echo\-seq\fR] [\fB\-\-icmp\-rest\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-code\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-checksum\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-echo\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-echo\-seq\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-rest\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-cur_hop_limit\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags\-m\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags\-o\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-router_lifetime\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-reachable_time\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-retrans_timer\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\-r\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\-s\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\-o\fR] [\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-target\fR] [\fB\-\-udp\-sport\fR] [\fB\-\-udp\-dport\fR] [\fB\-\-udp\-length\fR] [\fB\-\-udp\-checksum\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-sport\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-dport\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-seq\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-ack\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-data_off\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-cwr\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-ece\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-urg\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-ack\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-psh\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-rst\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-syn\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-fin\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-checksum\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-urgent\fR] [\fB\-\-tcp\-options\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-flags\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-qr\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-aa\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-tc\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-rd\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-ra\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-opcode\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-rcode\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-qdcount\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-ancount\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-nscount\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-arcount\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\-class\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-op\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-htype\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-hlen\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-hops\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-xid\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-flags\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-flags\-broadcast\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-ciaddr\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-yiaddr\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-siaddr\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-giaddr\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-chaddr\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-sname\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-cookie\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-msg_type\fR] [\fB\-\-dhcp\-options\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Encode a PacketSpec from field flags → stdout
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-iface\fR \fI<IFACE>\fR
Interface for send/recv
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format: raw|hex|text|json|jsonl
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Verbosity (repeatable: \-v info, \-vv debug, \-vvv trace)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-autofill\fR
Disable every autofill/derivation (unspecified numeric fields → 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Validate the crafted packet after encode (violations → exit 2)
.TP
\fB\-\-layer\fR \fI<KIND>\fR
declare encapsulation order (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-payload\fR \fI<VALUE>\fR
terminal payload bytes (hex:…, text:…, @FILE, @\-, repeat:NxHEX)
.TP
\fB\-\-eth\-dst\fR \fI<MAC>\fR
destination MAC (autofill: ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff)
.TP
\fB\-\-eth\-src\fR \fI<MAC>\fR
source MAC (autofill: interface MAC on send)
.TP
\fB\-\-eth\-type\fR \fI<INT>\fR
ethertype (autofill: derived from next layer)
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-htype\fR \fI<INT>\fR
hardware type (autofill: 1 ethernet)
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-ptype\fR \fI<INT>\fR
protocol type (autofill: 0x0800 ipv4)
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-hlen\fR \fI<INT>\fR
hardware address length (autofill: 6)
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-plen\fR \fI<INT>\fR
protocol address length (autofill: 4)
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-oper\fR \fI<INT>\fR
operation (autofill: 1 request)
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-sha\fR \fI<MAC>\fR
sender hardware address (autofill: 00:00:00:00:00:00)
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-spa\fR \fI<IP>\fR
sender protocol address
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-tha\fR \fI<MAC>\fR
target hardware address (autofill: 00:00:00:00:00:00)
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-tpa\fR \fI<IP>\fR
target protocol address (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-vlan\-pcp\fR \fI<INT>\fR
priority code point (0\-7, 3 bits)
.TP
\fB\-\-vlan\-dei\fR \fI<INT>\fR
drop eligible indicator (0/1, 1 bit)
.TP
\fB\-\-vlan\-vid\fR \fI<INT>\fR
VLAN identifier (0\-4095, 12 bits; 0 = priority tag)
.TP
\fB\-\-vlan\-type\fR \fI<INT>\fR
encapsulated ethertype (autofill: derived from next layer)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-ver\fR \fI<INT>\fR
version (autofill: 4)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-ihl\fR \fI<INT>\fR
header length in 32\-bit words (autofill: derived)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-tos\fR \fI<INT>\fR
type of service
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-total_len\fR \fI<INT>\fR
total length (autofill: computed)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-id\fR \fI<INT>\fR
identification (autofill: 0, deterministic)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-flags\fR \fI<BITS>\fR
flags aggregate [df,mf]; per\-bit subpaths flags.df / flags.mf
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-flags\-df\fR
set only the df bit of ipv4.flags (aggregate: \-\-ipv4\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-flags\-mf\fR
set only the mf bit of ipv4.flags (aggregate: \-\-ipv4\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-frag_off\fR \fI<INT>\fR
fragment offset
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-ttl\fR \fI<INT>\fR
time to live (autofill: 64)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-proto\fR \fI<INT>\fR
protocol (autofill: derived from next layer)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-checksum\fR \fI<INT>\fR
header checksum (autofill: computed)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-src\fR \fI<IP>\fR
source address (autofill: 127.0.0.1; interface primary on send)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-dst\fR \fI<IP>\fR
destination address (autofill: 127.0.0.1)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-options\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
options: eol,nop,rr:IP…,ssrr:IP…,lsrr:IP…,ts:FLAG,CNT, or hex:…
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv6\-ver\fR \fI<INT>\fR
version (autofill: 6)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv6\-traffic_class\fR \fI<INT>\fR
traffic class (top byte of the flow word)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv6\-flow_label\fR \fI<INT>\fR
flow label (low 20 bits of the flow word)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv6\-payload_len\fR \fI<INT>\fR
payload length in bytes (autofill: computed)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv6\-next_header\fR \fI<INT>\fR
next header (autofill: derived from next layer)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv6\-hop_limit\fR \fI<INT>\fR
hop limit (autofill: 64)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv6\-src\fR \fI<IPV6>\fR
source address (autofill: ::1)
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv6\-dst\fR \fI<IPV6>\fR
destination address (autofill: ::1)
.TP
\fB\-\-hopopts\-next_header\fR \fI<INT>\fR
next header protocol (autofill: derived from the next layer; 59 = no next header)
.TP
\fB\-\-hopopts\-len\fR \fI<INT>\fR
hdr_ext_len: header length in 8\-octet units minus 1 (autofill: exact over the padded region)
.TP
\fB\-\-hopopts\-options\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
raw TLV region after the 2\-byte prefix, zero\-padded to the 8\-octet grid on craft (hex on the CLI)
.TP
\fB\-\-dstopts\-next_header\fR \fI<INT>\fR
next header protocol (autofill: derived from the next layer; 59 = no next header)
.TP
\fB\-\-dstopts\-len\fR \fI<INT>\fR
hdr_ext_len: header length in 8\-octet units minus 1 (autofill: exact over the padded region)
.TP
\fB\-\-dstopts\-options\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
raw TLV region after the 2\-byte prefix, zero\-padded to the 8\-octet grid on craft (hex on the CLI)
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-next_header\fR \fI<INT>\fR
next header protocol (autofill: derived from the next layer; 59 = no next header)
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-len\fR \fI<INT>\fR
hdr_ext_len: header length in 8\-octet units minus 1 (autofill: exact over the padded region)
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-type\fR \fI<INT>\fR
routing type (0 = the deprecated RH0, 2 = home address)
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-segs_left\fR \fI<INT>\fR
segments left (not validated against the segment count)
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-segments\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
raw type\-specific region after the 4\-byte prefix (reserved bytes + 16\-byte addresses, hand\-built; hex on the CLI)
.TP
\fB\-\-frag\-next_header\fR \fI<INT>\fR
next header protocol of the fragmentable part (autofill: derived from the next layer)
.TP
\fB\-\-frag\-offset\fR \fI<INT>\fR
fragment offset in 8\-octet units (13 bits; over\-wide values mask)
.TP
\fB\-\-frag\-m\fR \fI<INT>\fR
more\-fragments flag (1 bit: 0 = last fragment)
.TP
\fB\-\-frag\-ident\fR \fI<INT>\fR
fragment identification (matches fragments of one packet)
.TP
\fB\-\-ah\-next_header\fR \fI<INT>\fR
next header protocol (autofill: derived from the next layer; 59 = no next header)
.TP
\fB\-\-ah\-len\fR \fI<INT>\fR
payload_len: AH length in 4\-octet units minus 2 (autofill: (octets/4)\-2, truncating — kept)
.TP
\fB\-\-ah\-spi\fR \fI<INT>\fR
security parameters index
.TP
\fB\-\-ah\-seq\fR \fI<INT>\fR
sequence number
.TP
\fB\-\-ah\-icv\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
integrity check value (raw, verbatim — never verified; hex on the CLI)
.TP
\fB\-\-esp\-spi\fR \fI<INT>\fR
security parameters index
.TP
\fB\-\-esp\-seq\fR \fI<INT>\fR
sequence number
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-type\fR \fI<INT>\fR
type (autofill: 8 echo request)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-code\fR \fI<INT>\fR
code (autofill: 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-checksum\fR \fI<INT>\fR
checksum over header+payload (autofill: computed)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-echo\-id\fR \fI<INT>\fR
echo identifier (types 0/8)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-echo\-seq\fR \fI<INT>\fR
echo sequence (types 0/8)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmp\-rest\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
raw 4\-byte rest of header (non\-echo types)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-type\fR \fI<INT>\fR
type (autofill: 128 echo request)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-code\fR \fI<INT>\fR
code (autofill: 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-checksum\fR \fI<INT>\fR
checksum over v6 pseudo\-header+message (autofill: computed)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-echo\-id\fR \fI<INT>\fR
echo identifier (types 128/129)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-echo\-seq\fR \fI<INT>\fR
echo sequence (types 128/129)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-rest\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
raw 4\-byte rest of header (non\-echo non\-NDP types)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-cur_hop_limit\fR \fI<INT>\fR
router advertisement: current hop limit
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags\fR \fI<BITS>\fR
router advertisement flags [m,o]; subpaths ndp.ra_flags.m / ndp.ra_flags.o
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags\-m\fR
set only the m bit of icmpv6.ndp.ra_flags (aggregate: \-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags\-o\fR
set only the o bit of icmpv6.ndp.ra_flags (aggregate: \-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-ra_flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-router_lifetime\fR \fI<INT>\fR
router advertisement: router lifetime (seconds)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-reachable_time\fR \fI<INT>\fR
router advertisement: reachable time (ms)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-retrans_timer\fR \fI<INT>\fR
router advertisement: retransmit timer (ms)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\fR \fI<BITS>\fR
neighbor advertisement flags [r,s,o]; subpaths ndp.na_flags.r / .s / .o
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\-r\fR
set only the r bit of icmpv6.ndp.na_flags (aggregate: \-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\-s\fR
set only the s bit of icmpv6.ndp.na_flags (aggregate: \-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags\-o\fR
set only the o bit of icmpv6.ndp.na_flags (aggregate: \-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-na_flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-icmpv6\-ndp\-target\fR \fI<IPV6>\fR
neighbor solicitation/advertisement: target address
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\-sport\fR \fI<INT>\fR
source port
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\-dport\fR \fI<INT>\fR
destination port
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\-length\fR \fI<INT>\fR
length incl. header (autofill: computed)
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\-checksum\fR \fI<INT>\fR
checksum over pseudo\-header+segment (autofill: computed)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-sport\fR \fI<INT>\fR
source port
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-dport\fR \fI<INT>\fR
destination port
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-seq\fR \fI<INT>\fR
sequence number
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-ack\fR \fI<INT>\fR
acknowledgment number
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-data_off\fR \fI<INT>\fR
data offset in 32\-bit words (autofill: derived)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\fR \fI<BITS>\fR
flag aggregate [cwr,ece,urg,ack,psh,rst,syn,fin]; subpaths flags.<bit>
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-cwr\fR
set only the cwr bit of tcp.flags (aggregate: \-\-tcp\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-ece\fR
set only the ece bit of tcp.flags (aggregate: \-\-tcp\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-urg\fR
set only the urg bit of tcp.flags (aggregate: \-\-tcp\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-ack\fR
set only the ack bit of tcp.flags (aggregate: \-\-tcp\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-psh\fR
set only the psh bit of tcp.flags (aggregate: \-\-tcp\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-rst\fR
set only the rst bit of tcp.flags (aggregate: \-\-tcp\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-syn\fR
set only the syn bit of tcp.flags (aggregate: \-\-tcp\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-flags\-fin\fR
set only the fin bit of tcp.flags (aggregate: \-\-tcp\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-window\fR \fI<INT>\fR
window (autofill: 64240)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-checksum\fR \fI<INT>\fR
checksum over pseudo\-header+segment (autofill: computed)
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-urgent\fR \fI<INT>\fR
urgent pointer
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\-options\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
options: eol,nop,mss:1460,ws:7,sackok,sack:L,R,…, or hex:…
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-id\fR \fI<INT>\fR
message id (craft: seeded by wrex query)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-flags\fR \fI<BITS>\fR
flag aggregate [qr,aa,tc,rd,ra]; subpaths flags.<bit>
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-qr\fR
set only the qr bit of dns.flags (aggregate: \-\-dns\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-aa\fR
set only the aa bit of dns.flags (aggregate: \-\-dns\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-tc\fR
set only the tc bit of dns.flags (aggregate: \-\-dns\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-rd\fR
set only the rd bit of dns.flags (aggregate: \-\-dns\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-flags\-ra\fR
set only the ra bit of dns.flags (aggregate: \-\-dns\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-opcode\fR \fI<INT>\fR
operation code (4 bits; 0 = QUERY)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-rcode\fR \fI<INT>\fR
response code (4 bits; 0 = NOERROR)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-qdcount\fR \fI<INT>\fR
question count (autofill: derived from the question)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-ancount\fR \fI<INT>\fR
answer count (autofill: 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-nscount\fR \fI<INT>\fR
authority count (autofill: 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-arcount\fR \fI<INT>\fR
additional count (autofill: 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-name\fR \fI<STRING>\fR
question name, dotted presentation form (example.com)
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-type\fR \fI<STRING>\fR
question type: A, NS, CNAME, SOA, PTR, MX, TXT, AAAA, SRV, OPT, ANY, TYPE<n> or a number
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\-class\fR \fI<STRING>\fR
question class: IN, CH, HS, ANY, CLASS<n> or a number
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-op\fR \fI<INT>\fR
message op: 1 BOOTREQUEST (client), 2 BOOTREPLY (server) (autofill: 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-htype\fR \fI<INT>\fR
hardware address type (autofill: 1 ethernet)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-hlen\fR \fI<INT>\fR
hardware address length (autofill: 6)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-hops\fR \fI<INT>\fR
relay hop count (autofill: 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-xid\fR \fI<INT>\fR
transaction id (autofill: 0, deterministic)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-secs\fR \fI<INT>\fR
seconds since client boot
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-flags\fR \fI<BITS>\fR
flag aggregate [broadcast] (0x8000); subpath flags.broadcast
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-flags\-broadcast\fR
set only the broadcast bit of dhcp.flags (aggregate: \-\-dhcp\-flags)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-ciaddr\fR \fI<IP>\fR
client IP address
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-yiaddr\fR \fI<IP>\fR
your (client) IP address
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-siaddr\fR \fI<IP>\fR
server IP address
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-giaddr\fR \fI<IP>\fR
gateway/relay IP address
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-chaddr\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
client hardware address (up to 16 bytes, zero\-padded)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-sname\fR \fI<STRING>\fR
server host name (NUL\-padded to 64; dissection trims at the first NUL)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-file\fR \fI<STRING>\fR
boot file name (NUL\-padded to 128; dissection trims at the first NUL)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-cookie\fR \fI<INT>\fR
magic cookie (autofill: 0x63825363)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-msg_type\fR \fI<STRING>\fR
DHCP message type, the hoisted option 53: discover|offer|request|decline|ack|nak|release|inform or 1\-8 (mutually exclusive with type: in \-\-dhcp\-options)
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp\-options\fR \fI<STRING>\fR
options list grammar: type:N, mask:IP, routers:IP…, dns:IP…, host:NAME, domain:NAME, req_ip:IP, lease:SECS, renew:SECS, rebind:SECS, server:IP, param_req:N…, max_msg:N, client_id:HEX, pad, hex:CODE:HEX (end marker appended automatically)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRA
LAYER ORDER:
  \-\-layer KIND declares encapsulation order (repeatable). Without it,
  layers are implied by the field flags present, ordered by rank;
  a sibling conflict (two rank\-30 kinds, or arp+ipv4) errors with a
  hint to pass \-\-layer. Field flags for a kind you did not declare
  require \-\-layer KIND.

SEMANTICS:
  Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept unvalidated;
  \-\-strict re\-validates the crafted packet (violations exit 2).
  Every settable field, type, default and bit name: wrex fields [KIND].

EXAMPLES:
  # 46\-byte golden frame; autofill derives eth.type, ipv4.total_len,
  # ipv4.checksum, udp.length and udp.checksum from the packet
  wrex craft \-\-format hex \-\-layer eth \-\-layer ipv4 \-\-layer udp \\
    \-\-eth\-dst=ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff \-\-ipv4\-src=127.0.0.1 \-\-ipv4\-dst=127.0.0.1 \\
    \-\-udp\-sport=4444 \-\-udp\-dport=5555 \-\-payload=hex:deadbeef

  # implied mode: the same bytes without \-\-layer (layers come from flags)
  wrex craft \-\-format hex \\
    \-\-eth\-dst=ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff \-\-ipv4\-src=127.0.0.1 \-\-ipv4\-dst=127.0.0.1 \\
    \-\-udp\-sport=4444 \-\-udp\-dport=5555 \-\-payload=hex:deadbeef

  # send on an interface (needs CAP_NET_RAW; send stacks start with eth)
  wrex send \-i lo \-\-layer eth \-\-layer ipv4 \-\-layer udp \\
    \-\-ipv4\-src=127.0.0.1 \-\-ipv4\-dst=127.0.0.1 \\
    \-\-udp\-sport=1 \-\-udp\-dport=2 \-\-payload=hex:aa

  # no field flags + piped stdin: raw stdin bytes are sent as\-is
